{{- /*
bun-resolve.sh.tmpl — the shared bun resolution ladder for chezmoi scripts that
build with bun. Emits plain shell; it takes no data argument.

.ci/lib/bun.sh is the same ladder for CI scripts, which run outside chezmoi's
templating and so cannot include this partial. The two must stay rung-for-rung
identical. If you change one, change the other.

THE LADDER, in order:

  1  bun already on PATH
  2  $HOME/.local/bin/bun                                    public link
  3  $HOME/.local/lib/commands/current/bun/bun               current generation
  4  $HOME/.local/share/chezmoi-commands/incomplete/bun/bun  staging

CONTRACT. On success it sets BUN_BIN to the resolved absolute path, BUN_DIR to
that binary's directory, and PREPENDS BUN_DIR to PATH. When no rung matches it
leaves BUN_BIN and BUN_DIR empty and leaves PATH untouched — the caller decides
whether an absent bun is fatal, a skip, or a fallback to another toolchain. The
partial never exits, prints, or fails on its own.

WHY IT PREPENDS PATH INSTEAD OF ONLY EXPORTING BUN_BIN. `vp run build` spawns
`bun build --compile` as a subprocess, and that subprocess resolves `bun` from
PATH, not from any variable this script sets. An absolute BUN_BIN alone would
therefore build under mise and still fail one level down on a host where bun is
not on PATH. This is settled as KTD3 in the plan under docs/plans/.

WHY THE STAGING PATH IS THE LAST RUNG RATHER THAN NO RUNG. The public
~/.local/bin/bun link is created by run_after_90-activate-command-links, which
needs the command-reconcile binary that 00-tools/10-build-command-reconcile
builds. On a fresh host's first apply the only bun that exists is the one an
external just wrote to the staging directory, so the build script must be able
to see it. The MISE_BIN ladder in that same script already has the equivalent
rung, for the same reason.

The PATH guard is the repo's `case ":$PATH:"` idiom, so a directory already on
PATH (rung 1, in particular) is not appended a second time. BUN_DIR is derived
with a parameter expansion rather than `dirname` so the partial needs nothing on
PATH to resolve bun — the callers run before any PATH is guaranteed.
*/ -}}
BUN_BIN=""
BUN_DIR=""
for bun_candidate in \
  "$(command -v bun 2>/dev/null || true)" \
  "$HOME/.local/bin/bun" \
  "$HOME/.local/lib/commands/current/bun/bun" \
  "$HOME/.local/share/chezmoi-commands/incomplete/bun/bun"; do
  if [[ -n "$bun_candidate" && -x "$bun_candidate" ]]; then
    BUN_BIN="$bun_candidate"
    break
  fi
done
unset bun_candidate
if [[ -n "$BUN_BIN" ]]; then
  case "$BUN_BIN" in
    */*) BUN_DIR="${BUN_BIN%/*}" ;;
    *) BUN_DIR="" ;;
  esac
  if [[ -n "$BUN_DIR" ]]; then
    case ":$PATH:" in
      *":$BUN_DIR:"*) ;;
      *) PATH="$BUN_DIR:$PATH" ;;
    esac
    export PATH
  fi
fi
